The app is extracted and updated by one caller at a time.

Opening the app and a wake for background refresh that finds the app launched
with no window both make sure the app is in place before booting PHP. Run side
by side, both could copy the bundle into the same directory at once. The second
caller now waits for the first, then finds the app in place and copies nothing.

--- a/vendor/nativephp/mobile/resources/xcode/NativePHP/AppUpdateManager.swift
+++ b/vendor/nativephp/mobile/resources/xcode/NativePHP/AppUpdateManager.swift
@@ -12,1 +12,2 @@
     private var appReady = false
+    private let ensuring = NSLock()
@@ -31,2 +32,5 @@
     func ensureAppExists() -> Bool {
         print("📦 AppUpdateManager.ensureAppExists() starting")
+
+        ensuring.lock()
+        defer { ensuring.unlock() }
